gent identity; the user is a separate subject field and the actor stays the agent role.\",\n          \"note\": \"User carried as separate subject field\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Permissions are bound to the agent principal in IaC or RBAC, so revoking that principal alone removes the agent's access without disabling the user.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find IAM policies, RoleBindings, or grants in Terraform, Helm, or Kubernetes YAML. 2) Check they bind to the agent principal, not to a user, group, or shared role. 3) Check that removing that binding alone would cut the agent's access. 4) Answer no if access depends on the user's grants or a shared credential. Answer unknown if permissions are not defined in this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/iam.tf:3\",\n          \"quote\": \"resource \\\"aws_iam_role\\\" \\\"runtime\\\" {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for user-bound grants; permissions attach to the runtime role and removing it cuts agent access without touching users.\",\n          \"note\": \"Permissions bind to the agent role in terraform\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Agent has its own service account and IAM role separate from users.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Drill disabling the role without affecting staff or patient sessions.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\",\n      \"challenge\": {\n        \"verdict\": \"upheld\",\n        \"note\": \"I found no failing control; the main weakness is that the eligibility token exchange encodes the patient only in the scope string rather than as a true delegated subject.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A02\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"All six identity fields\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Check that every action records the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context. Look at successful, denied, failed, and background actions, not just the main request path.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Identity labels taken from what the model supplies\",\n          \"owner\": \"A04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent-type-id not computed as a hash of its identity inputs\",\n          \"owner\": \"A03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent able to erase or rewrite its own audit history\",\n          \"owner\": \"E10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Sub-agent record missing its parent link or parent prompt\",\n          \"owner\": \"A06\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts\",\n          \"line\": 8,\n          \"note\": \"Audit schema has all six fields\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.1\",\n          \"check\": \"The audit record schema has all six fields: accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the audit record schema or the function that writes audit entries. 2) Check for each of the six: accountable party, operational owner, tenant, `agent.type.id`, `agent.instance.id`, trace context (`traceparent` or trace and span IDs). 3) Answer no if any one is missing from the schema or never set.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts:8\",\n          \"quote\": \"export const IdentityFields = z.object({\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Checked the schema lists accountableParty, operationalOwner, tenantId, agentTypeId, agentInstanceId and traceparent as required.\",\n          \"note\": \"Audit schema has all six fields\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.2\",\n          \"check\": 