ghts against the approved baseline, with each of these covered.\",\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find the drift check job or tool. 2) List what it compares: images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, self-hosted weights. 3) Check each is compared with the approved baseline, not with the live state itself. 4) Answer no if any category is missing or excluded. Answer unknown if drift detection runs in an outside platform.\",\n   \"met\": \"no\",\n   \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml:29\",\n   \"quote\": \"      - name: Prompt digests match the release manifest\",\n   \"counter_search\": \"\",\n   \"note\": \"[challenge] The only baseline comparison is a CI step checking prompt file hashes and harness version against release/manifest.json. It reads repo files, not running state. Nothing compares running images, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies or self-hosted weights. The repo has no drift tool, and the README names no outside platform that does this.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"C04.2\",\n   \"check\": \"The drift check runs per agent deployment, on a schedule or on change events.\",\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find what triggers the drift check: cron or CI schedule, admission webhook, or change events. 2) Check it runs for each agent deployment, not once for the fleet or only by hand. 3) Answer no if it is manual-only or covers only some deployments. Answer unknown if scheduling is set outside this repo.\",\n   \"met\": \"unknown\",\n   \"evidence\": \"\",\n   \"quote\": \"\",\n   \"counter_search\": \"\",\n   \"note\": \"[challenge: unclear] CI triggers only on PR and push, with no schedule. The only CronJob (k8s/deployment.yaml:115) is the reminders worker. No per-deployment drift job exists in the repo. Scheduling could live outside the repo, so this can't be confirmed.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"C04.3\",\n   \"check\": \"Detected drift triggers an alert and a set response (block, quarantine, or rollback) defined in config, with a time limit.\",\n   \"verify\": \"1) Open the drift check's result handling. 2) Check drift raises an alert and triggers a response set in config: block, quarantine, or rollback. 3) Check a time limit is set. 4) Answer no if drift only logs, the response or time limit is missing, or a check error is treated as no drift.\",\n   \"met\": \"unknown\",\n   \"evidence\": \"\",\n   \"quote\": \"\",\n   \"counter_search\": \"\",\n   \"note\": \"[challenge: unclear] A mismatch only fails the CI build. There is no alert, no quarantine or rollback response in config, and no time limit. Without a drift check in the repo, there is no result handling to evaluate.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"red_flags_found\": [\n  \".github/workflows/ci.yml:29 The only baseline comparison is a CI step checking prompt file hashes and harness version against release/manifest.json. It reads repo files, not running state. Nothing compares running images, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies or self-hosted weights. The repo has no drift tool, and the README names no outside platform that does this.\"\n ],\n \"violates\": [\n  \"Compare running images, harness settings, prompts, MCP server lists, permissions, network policies, and self-hosted model weights against their approved baseline\"\n ],\n \"also_affects\": [],\n \"summary\": \"No runtime drift check, alert or response is shown in the repo.\",\n \"next_step\": \"Show the drift job covering image, prompts, tool list, permissions and egress, and its response time.\",\n \"lead_role\": \"operations\",\n \"challenge\": {\n  \"verdict\": \"failed\",\n  \"note\": \"The repo's only baseline comparison is a CI check of prompt digests and harness version, so running images, MCP lists, permissions, network policies and weights are never compared.\"\n }\n}\nNC [{\"problem\": \"Hosted model changing behind a fixed name\", \"owner\": \"C05\"}, {\"problem\": \"A tool server changing its description or schema after approval\", \"owner\": \"E03\"}, {\"p